---
/**
 * Popover Component
 *
 * STATUS: KEPT AS REACT (src/components/ui/popover.tsx)
 *
 * RATIONALE FOR KEEPING AS REACT:
 * This component uses @radix-ui/react-popover which provides:
 * - Portal rendering for proper z-index layering
 * - Complex positioning logic (top, bottom, left, right with align options)
 * - Trigger state management (click to toggle)
 * - Optional arrow/pointer indicators
 * - ARIA attributes and full accessibility support (role="dialog")
 * - Composable sub-components (Root, Trigger, Content, Anchor)
 * - Animated open/close transitions
 * - Focus management (focus trap when open)
 * - Click outside to close functionality
 * - Escape key to close
 * - Collision detection to keep popover visible in viewport
 *
 * Conversion Complexity Analysis:
 * - Estimated ~500-700 lines of vanilla JS/Alpine.js to replicate
 * - Extensive accessibility testing required
 * - Custom portal positioning implementation needed
 * - Focus trap logic and click-outside handling to implement from scratch
 * - NOT currently used in the codebase (grep confirmed no usage)
 * - Should consider if this component is actually needed
 *
 * Decision: Keep as React component with @astrojs/react integration
 * Use with `client:load` directive when needed in Astro pages
 *
 * USAGE IN ASTRO PAGES:
 * ```astro
 * ---
 * import { Popover, PopoverTrigger, PopoverContent } from '@/components/ui/popover';
 * ---
 *
 * <Popover client:load>
 *   <PopoverTrigger>Open Popover</PopoverTrigger>
 *   <PopoverContent>
 *     <p>This is popover content</p>
 *   </PopoverContent>
 * </Popover>
 * ```
 *
 * PROPS:
 * - open?: boolean - Controlled open state
 * - defaultOpen?: boolean - Uncontrolled default open state
 * - onOpenChange?: (open: boolean) => void - Callback when open state changes
 * - modal?: boolean - Whether to trap focus inside popover (default: true)
 * - side?: 'top' | 'right' | 'bottom' | 'left' - Position relative to trigger
 * - sideOffset?: number - Distance from trigger in px (default: 4)
 * - align?: 'start' | 'center' | 'end' - Alignment along the side (default: "center")
 * - alignOffset?: number - Offset from alignment position
 * - arrowPadding?: number - Padding between arrow and trigger edges
 * - avoidCollisions?: boolean - Enable collision detection
 *
 * ALTERNATIVES:
 * 1. Native HTML details/summary (simple, no positioning control):
 *    ```astro
 *    <details class="popover">
 *      <summary>Toggle</summary>
 *      <p>Content</p>
 *    </details>
 *    ```
 *
 * 2. Dropdown menu component (similar functionality):
 *    ```astro
 *    ---
 *    import { DropdownMenu, DropdownMenuTrigger, DropdownMenuContent } from '@/components/ui/dropdown-menu';
 *    ---
 *    ```
 *
 * 3. Tippy.js (lightweight alternative to Radix):
 *    ```bash
 *    npx astro add tippy.js
 *    ```
 *
 * USAGE NOTE:
 * This component is not currently used in the codebase. Consider whether
 * a simpler alternative (like DropdownMenu or Dialog) would be more appropriate
 * for your use case before implementing Popover.
 */
